  "summary_en": "Hungary's national AI strategy for 2020–2030, a living document with an action plan to 2025. It sets GDP, productivity and workforce targets and covers data economy, R&D, skills, infrastructure and an ethics code. Sector programmes include autonomous vehicles (Zalaegerszeg testbed), manufacturing, agriculture and defence. Governance of physical AI is secondary.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Targets for 2030: 15% AI-induced GDP growth, 26% productivity growth, and 1 million citizens in higher value-added jobs.",
   "Create a National Data Asset Agency, a data marketplace and a public data portal.",
   "Develop an AI Ethics Code and an AI Regulatory and Ethics Knowledge Centre (MISZET); consider AI registers and liability rules.",
   "Transformative programme to make Hungary Europe's leading centre for autonomous vehicle development and testing.",
   "Establish an AI National Laboratory and sandbox/testbed infrastructure; review the strategy at least every two years."
